WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.200
After the first visit,

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.580
how can we keep loving someone who’s

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:06.900
grieving?

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.740
Romans twelve puts shared sorrow beside constant

5
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.200
prayer,

6
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.740
contributing to needs,

7
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.280
and seeking hospitality.

8
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.960
Love takes practical shape.

9
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.160
Grief can make ordinary tasks feel heavy.

10
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.720
Ask what would help,

11
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.080
and offer something you can actually do.

12
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.740
Could I bring dinner tomorrow?

13
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.360
Would it help if I washed

14
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:27.800
the dishes?

15
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.190
A specific offer can make answering easier.

16
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.330
Keep praying,

17
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.530
and check in again.

18
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.320
Give them room to say no,

19
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.980
or to need something different.

20
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.220
We serve the Lord as we care

21
00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.040
for his people.

22
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.140
You don’t have to remove the grief

23
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.020
to help carry the ordinary weight

24
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.560
of the day.
